$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=tm2comptel  LOC_AFTER=?

* TM2CompT for explicit tuples: the machine M with the alphabet bijections I, J and the time function T witnesses that F is computed with input encoding D (alphabet A) and output encoding G (alphabet B) if and only if M is a bundled finite machine, the bijections and the time function have the right types, and on every input a the machine outputs the encoded value of F within time of the input length.

